      "originalHtml": "<p><span class=\"b\">Câu</span><span class=\"b\"> </span><span class=\"b\">36:</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>You are a speculator who sells a call option on Swiss francs for a premium of $.06, with an exercise price of $.64. The option will not be exercised until the expiration date, if at all. If the spot rate of the Swiss franc is $.69 on the expiration date, your net profit per unit, assuming that you have to buy Swiss francs in the market to fulfill your obligation, is:</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">A.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>−$.02.<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">B. </span>−$.01.<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b u\">C.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>$.01.<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">D.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>$.02.</p>\n<p><span class=\"b i\">SOLUTION:</span><span class=\"b i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">Net</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">profit</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">per</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">unit</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">=</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">$.64</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">+</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">$.06</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">−</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">$.69</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">=</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">$.01.</span></p>"
