      "originalHtml": "<p><span class=\"b\">Câu</span><span class=\"b\"> </span><span class=\"b\">37:</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>You are a speculator who sells a put option on Canadian dollars for a premium of $.03 per unit, with an exercise price of</p>\n<p>$.86. The option will not be exercised until the expiration date, if at all. If the spot rate of the Canadian dollar is $.78 on the expiration date, your net profit per unit is:</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">A.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>−$.08.<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">B. </span>−$.03.<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">C.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>$.05.<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b u\">D.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>none of the above</p>\n<p><span class=\"b i\">SOLUTION:</span><span class=\"b i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">Net</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">profit</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">=</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">$.78</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">+</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">$.03</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">−</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">$.86</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">=</span><span class=\"i\"> </span><span class=\"i\">−$.05.</span></p>"
