      "originalHtml": "<p><span class=\"b\">Câu</span><span class=\"b\"> </span><span class=\"b\">22:</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>Assume that the euro&#x27;s interest rates are higher than U.S. interest rates, and that interest rate parity exists. Which of the following is true?</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">A.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>Americans using covered interest arbitrage earn the same rate of return as Germans who attempt covered interest arbitrage</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">B.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>Americans who invest in the U.S. earn the same rate of return as Germans who attempt covered interest arbitrage.</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">C.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>Americans who invest in the U.S. earn the same rate of return as Germans who invest in Germany</p>\n<p><span class=\"b u\">D.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>None of the above</p>"
