      "title": "Câu 24:",
      "context": "TCQT_C6",
      "text": "Câu 24: Assume that British interest rates are higher than U.S. rates, and that the spot rate equals the forward rate. Covered interest arbitrage puts pressure on the pound's spot rate, and pressure on the pound's forward rate.\nA. downward; downward B. downward; upward C. upward; downward D. upward; upward",
      "frontHtml": "<p><span class=\"b\">Câu</span><span class=\"b\"> </span><span class=\"b\">24:</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>Assume that British interest rates are higher than U.S. rates, and that the spot rate equals the forward rate. Covered interest arbitrage puts <span class=\"tab\"></span>pressure on the pound&#x27;s spot rate, and <span class=\"tab\"></span>pressure on the pound&#x27;s forward rate.</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">A.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>downward; downward<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">B.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>downward; upward<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">C.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>upward; downward<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">D.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>upward; upward</p>",
