      "text": "Câu 16: Assume that the U.S. and Chile nominal interest rates are equal. Then, the U.S. nominal interest rate decreases while the Chilean nominal interest rate remains stable. According to the international Fisher effect, this implies expectations of than before, and that the Chilean peso should against the dollar\nA. lower U.S. inflation; depreciate B. lower U.S. inflation; appreciate\nC. higher U.S. inflation; depreciate D. higher U.S. inflation; appreciate",
