      "context": "TCQT_C7",
      "text": "Câu 22: The inflation rate in the U.S. is 3%, while the inflation rate in Japan is 10%. The current exchange rate for the Japanese yen (¥) is $0.0075. After supply and demand for the Japanese yen has adjusted in the manner suggested by purchasing power parity, the new exchange rate for the yen will be:\nA. $0.0076. B. $0.0073 C. $0.0070 D. $0.0066",
