      "originalHtml": "<p><span class=\"b\">Câu</span><span class=\"b\"> </span><span class=\"b\">30:</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>Which of the following theories suggests that the percentage difference between the forward rate and the spot rate depends on the interest rate differential between two countries?</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">A.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>purchasing power parity (PPP)<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">B.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>triangular arbitrage</p>\n<p><img class=\"card-image\" src=\"data/media/image3.png\" alt=\"Hinh cau hoi\"><span class=\"b\">C.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>international Fisher effect (IFE)<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b u\">D.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>interest rate parity (IRP).</p>"
