      "frontHtml": "<p><span class=\"b\">Câu</span><span class=\"b\"> </span><span class=\"b\">33:</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>The following regression analysis was conducted for the inflation rate information and exchange rate of the British pound: Regression results indicate that a0 = 0 and a1 = 1. Therefore:</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">A.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>purchasing power parity holds.</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">B.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>purchasing power parity overestimated the exchange rate change during the period under examination</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">C.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>purchasing power parity underestimated the exchange rate change during the period under examination</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">D.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>purchasing power parity will overestimate the exchange rate change of the British pound in the future</p>",
      "originalHtml": "<p><span class=\"b\">Câu</span><span class=\"b\"> </span><span class=\"b\">33:</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>The following regression analysis was conducted for the inflation rate information and exchange rate of the British pound: Regression results indicate that a0 = 0 and a1 = 1. Therefore:</p>\n<p><span class=\"b u\">A.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>purchasing power parity holds.</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">B.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>purchasing power parity overestimated the exchange rate change during the period under examination</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">C.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>purchasing power parity underestimated the exchange rate change during the period under examination</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">D.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>purchasing power parity will overestimate the exchange rate change of the British pound in the future</p>"
