      "text": "Câu 40: Assume that the interest rate offered on pounds is 5% and the pound is expected to depreciate by 1.5%. For the international Fisher effect (IFE) to hold between the U.K. and the U.S., the U.S. interest rate should be .\nA. 3.43% B. 5.68% C. 6.5% D. 7.3%",
