      "originalHtml": "<p><span class=\"b\">Câu</span><span class=\"b\"> </span><span class=\"b\">25:</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>The U.S. inflation rate is expected to be 4 percent over the next year, while the European inflation rate is expected to be 3 percent. The current spot rate of the euro is $1.03. Using purchasing power parity, the expected spot rate at the end of one year is $<span class=\"u\"><span class=\"tab\"></span></span>.</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">A.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>1.02<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">B.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>1.03<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b u\">C.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>1.04<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">D.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>None of the above</p>"
