      "originalHtml": "<p><span class=\"b\">Câu 27: </span>If both interest rate parity and the international Fisher effect hold, then between the forward rate and the spot rate, the <span class=\"u\"><span class=\"tab\"></span></span> rate should provide more accurate forecasts for currencies in <span class=\"u\"><span class=\"tab\"></span></span>-inflation countries</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">A.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>spot; high<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">B. </span>spot; low<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b u\">C.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>forward; high<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">D.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>forward; low</p>"
