      "originalHtml": "<p><span class=\"b\">Câu 10: </span>Assume that the British pound and Swiss franc are highly correlated. A U.S. firm anticipates the equivalent of $1 million cash outflows in francs and the equivalent of $1 million cash outflows in pounds. During a <span class=\"u\"><span class=\"tab\"></span></span>cycle, the firm is <span class=\"u\"><span class=\"tab\"></span></span>affected by its exposure</p>\n<p><span class=\"b u\">A.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>strong dollar; favorably<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">B.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>weak dollar; not</p>\n<p><span class=\"b\">C.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>strong dollar; not<span class=\"tab\"></span><span class=\"b\">D.</span><span class=\"b\"> </span>weak dollar; favorably</p>"
