      "originalHtml": "<p>1: BIDV can borrow either AUD10 million or $5 million. The current spot rate of the AUD is $0.48 and AUD will increase to $0.5 in the next 5 days. Furthermore, BIDV expects the spot rate of the euro to be $1.10 in 90 days. Today, U.S. Dollar ($) lending rate is 7.10% and borrowing rate is 7.50%. On the other hand, AUD lending rate is 6.80% and borrowing rate is 7.25%. If BIDV&#x27;s forecast is correct, what will its dollar profit be from speculation over the five-day period? (assuming it does not use any of its existing consumer deposits to capitalize on its expectations) (Write down the number only, no currency symbol, round up to 0 decimal number, assume that 1 year has 360 days) <span class=\"b\">208,044</span></p>"
